> Looking at the official grammar (and confirming this with the official
> parser), I don't think that's a bug in jbofi'e.  It appears that a bare
> {lerfu} string cannot have any free modifiers attached to it

The PEG parser however does allow it, except when the free modifier is
"(number / lerfu-string) MAI", which does require the BOI to separate
one lerfu-string from another or from the number.

